###############################################################################
# FX rates: all pairs, filters, source and provider
#
# Each rate shows its source (live / cache / fallback), the provider, when the
# provider published it (providerUpdatedAt) and when we stored it (refreshedAt).
###############################################################################

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1

### All 20 pairs between the 5 stablecoins, plus provider attribution
GET {{api}}/rates

### Everything 1 USDx buys
GET {{api}}/rates?from=USDx

### What each currency is worth in cNGN
GET {{api}}/rates?to=cNGN

### A single pair: cNGN to cGHS (derived from two USD quotes)
GET {{api}}/rates?from=cNGN&to=cGHS

### Same currency: rate is exactly 1
GET {{api}}/rates?from=EURx&to=EURx

### Unsupported currency
# Expect 400
GET {{api}}/rates?from=BTC

###############################################################################
# Trying the fallback chain
#
# Point the provider at an unreachable address and make stored rates count as
# stale immediately, then restart the API (bash):
#   FX_PROVIDER_URL=http://10.255.255.1/ FX_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=1 docker compose up -d api
# The background refresh at startup times out (3 s) and starts a 60 s backoff,
# so GET /rates answers immediately with source "cache": the last stored live
# rates. Swaps and transfers keep working and record rateSource "cache".
# Restore with: docker compose up -d api
###############################################################################
